@!@
# This is registered via `ucs_registerLDAPExtension --acl` (settings/ldapacl), which is the only
# existing mechanism that replicates a slapd.conf.d subfile domain-wide and activates it on the
# Primary (and Backup/Replica) Directory Node regardless of which host installs this app - exactly
# what's needed here, since univention-office365 is sometimes installed on a Backup Directory Node
# while this must take effect on the Primary. settings/ldapacl doesn't actually validate that the
# registered content is ACL syntax (it just writes the file and runs `slaptest -u` on the whole
# resulting slapd.conf), so this deliberately repurposes it to ship an overlay directive instead.
#
# Extend LDAP referential integrity to univentionMicrosoft365GroupOwners: group owners are stored
# as a DN reference on the group object in UDM, but this reference was never updated/removed when
# the referenced user got deleted, renamed, or moved. This declares its own refint overlay instance
# (rather than appending to core's `refint_attributes uniqueMember` in 40univention-ldap-server_database)
# because several other overlays are configured after that line in the same file; a bare
# refint_attributes line there would attach to whichever overlay is textually last, not to refint.
if configRegistry.is_true('ldap/refint', True) and configRegistry.get('server/role') == 'domaincontroller_master':
    print('overlay\t\trefint')
    print('refint_attributes\t\tuniventionMicrosoft365GroupOwners')
@!@
